otek-perfex-linux-tracker (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed the taskbar/dock/Alt-Tab icon showing a generic placeholder:
    the .desktop file's filename must exactly match the GTK Application's
    application_id for GNOME Shell to resolve its Icon= for window-list
    purposes (a different lookup than the app-grid entry, which was
    already working). Renamed otek-perfex-linux-tracker.desktop to
    today.otek.perfex_linux_tracker.desktop to match application_id
    "today.otek.perfex_linux_tracker" - confirmed against
    today.otek.currency_converter, whose own .desktop filename already
    matches its application_id the same way.

 -- Ömer Teknoloji <support@otek.today>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

otek-perfex-linux-tracker (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Aggregation: unified window/browser-tab grouping to (app class, exact
    title), with undersized groups merged into the largest sibling of the
    same app class instead of being dropped, and a lone undersized group
    with no sibling fully discarded as the only remaining drop case.
  * GTK4 UI follows the system light/dark theme (no hardcoded colors);
    close button now hides the window instead of quitting, matching the
    Clockify-proven pattern, gated on the tray being available.
  * Added optional top-bar tray indicator (Start/Stop/Show/Quit), backed
    by a separate GTK3 AyatanaAppIndicator3 helper subprocess talking to
    the main GTK4 process over stdin/stdout JSON - the same library
    combination confirmed in use by Upwork, VS Code, Zoom, and
    OnlyOffice/Jitsi on this platform.
  * Tray icon now correctly resolves via an explicit icon theme path
    (previously showed a generic placeholder) and swaps between
    active/inactive PNGs by tracking state.
  * Upgraded app icon to 512x512.

 -- Ömer Teknoloji <support@otek.today>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

otek-perfex-linux-tracker (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: passive focus-based session tracking against one
    Perfex CRM task, reconciled and submitted as a batch of timesheet
    entries at Stop via the taskimportperfexcrm module's new
    /timesheets_bulk endpoint.
  * Wayland-only window-focus polling via the window-calls-extended
    GNOME Shell extension.
  * Optional per-URL browser-tab granularity via a local HTTP server
    fed by PerfexCRMChromeExtension/PerfexCRMFirefoxExtension.
  * Crash-safe SQLite session log with orphaned-session recovery.

 -- Ömer Teknoloji <support@otek.today>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
